.TH MARBOR\-MODELS 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor\-models \- fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor models
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pull <node> <model>
start pulling a model onto a node (async - does not wait for completion)
.TP
.B delete <node> <model>
delete a model from a node's local storage
.TP
.B unload <node> <model>
unload a model from a node's warm state
.TP
.B list <node>
list models present on a node's local storage (per\-node, not the fleet\-wide aggregate above)
.TP
.B fleet
fleet residency with VRAM totals and drift (same live data as bare models, filterable)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-drifted-only
only show models where nodes disagree on digest
.RE
.TP
.B search
search Hugging Face models (P\-A2-06c)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-q string
search query
.TP
.B \-\-runtime string
filter by runtime compatibility
.TP
.B \-\-sort string
downloads (default), likes, newest, or oldest
.RE
.TP
.B repo <owner/name>
show Hugging Face repo detail with per\-node fit (P\-A2-06c)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-node string
node to check fit/downloaded\-status against
.TP
.B \-\-runtime string
runtime to size variants for
.TP
.B \-\-ctx int
context window in tokens for VRAM sizing (0 = server default 8192)
.RE
.TP
.B pull\-progress <node> <model>
show a point\-in-time snapshot of an active pull (P\-A2-08b)
.TP
.B cancel\-pull <node> <model>
cancel an in\-flight pull (P\-A2-08b)
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor\fR(1)
